#slide("VALIDATION", "Test the platform on your work.", "Use a small acceptance set spanning the capabilities you need.", (("Documents + data","Create a briefing with verifiable citations; reconcile a workbook and preserve formulas."),("Enterprise actions","Read and update a test record with correct identity, permissions and approval behaviour."),("Recurring execution","Run a scheduled task through failures, retries and notification. Check for duplicate writes."),), "Set task-specific quality, reliability, cost and review thresholds before comparing options.", (("NIST, Generative AI Profile, AI 600-1 (2024)","https://www.nist.gov/publications/artificial-intelligence-risk-management-framework-generative-artificial-intelligence"),), "Illustrative acceptance tasks. Passing them supports only the capabilities and conditions actually tested.")
#slide("ENABLEMENT", "Train people to delegate and review.", "Teach a repeatable method using their own work.", (("Describe","State the objective, inputs, output format, constraints and how completion will be judged."),("Verify","Check facts, calculations, sources and proposed actions. Learn when to request specialist help."),("Reuse","Turn validated instructions into shared examples; nominate an owner before scheduling or broad distribution."),), "Measure whether training produces independently completed, reviewed tasks.", (("Prosus, The Coming Age of AI Colleagues (2026; company-reported)","https://staticcontents.investis.com/media/p/prosus/the-coming-age-of-ai-colleagues/report.html"),("McKinsey, The State of AI (2026; respondent survey)","https://www.mckinsey.com/capabilities/quantumblack/our-insights/the-state-of-ai"),), "Proposed training curriculum, informed by enterprise adoption and workflow-redesign evidence.")
#slide("DELIVERY", "Expand through evidence and shared capabilities.", "Use decision gates rather than assuming every experiment should become production.", (("Establish","Name a sponsor and platform owner. Baseline tasks, approve data boundaries and connect initial systems."),("Validate","Train an initial group. Test useful tasks and address capability gaps. Proceed when quality and controls meet agreed thresholds."),("Expand","Share validated methods, add reusable integrations and support departmental ownership. Retire unsuccessful agents."),), "Scale the capabilities that enable useful work, then expand the work they support.", (("Prosus, The Coming Age of AI Colleagues (2026; company-reported)","https://staticcontents.investis.com/media/p/prosus/the-coming-age-of-ai-colleagues/report.html"),("NIST, Generative AI Profile, AI 600-1 (2024)","https://www.nist.gov/publications/artificial-intelligence-risk-management-framework-generative-artificial-intelligence"),), "Proposed rollout sequence. Scope and timing should follow organisational readiness.")
#slide("OUTCOMES", "Measure accepted work and realised value.", "Usage shows adoption. Outcomes show whether the investment is worthwhile.", (("Delivery","Accepted completion rate, task volume, quality checks, human review and recovery effort."),("Economics","Total operating cost; net time saved after review; cost per accepted task; evidenced revenue or cash effects."),("Adoption","Active repeat users, independently completed tasks and reuse of approved integrations and instructions."),), "Keep capacity released, cash savings and revenue gains as separate measures.", (("McKinsey, The State of AI (2026; respondent survey)","https://www.mckinsey.com/capabilities/quantumblack/our-insights/the-state-of-ai"),("NIST, Generative AI Profile, AI 600-1 (2024)","https://www.nist.gov/publications/artificial-intelligence-risk-management-framework-generative-artificial-intelligence"),), "Proposed scorecard. Self-reported time savings need verification before financial attribution.")
